{
  // Mirrors trade-verdict's Phase 0 TypeScript adoption pass (see that
  // repo's CLAUDE.md, "Engineering: TypeScript adoption path" — Aug 14,
  // 2026) into this repo, the real backend (Aug 16, 2026). JSDoc + checkJs
  // only: no .ts files, no build step, ever. Run with `tsc --noEmit` (or
  // `npx tsc`, TypeScript is not a committed devDependency here).
  //
  // Scope is deliberately narrow — gates-extended.js only — same scope
  // trade-verdict's own Phase 0 used, kept low-risk on purpose. server.js
  // (where the real /analyze handler, evaluateProxyStatus(), and
  // evaluateGate1() actually live) and credits.js are NOT covered yet
  // (untyped Express/Stripe/Supabase surface, much higher noise) — a
  // natural follow-up once this proves out, not part of this pass. This
  // repo has no shared/ subdirectory (that's a trade-verdict/frontend-only
  // concept), so this tsconfig's scope is just the one file plus types.js.
  //
  // Phase 2 (real .ts, transpile-only) mirrored in Aug 16, 2026, following
  // trade-verdict's own gates-extended.ts conversion — see
  // tsconfig.build.json for the emit config. gates-extended.js is now
  // authored as gates-extended.ts; types.js stays exactly as it was
  // (JSDoc-only, Phase 0 style) since gates-extended.ts doesn't import
  // from it at all — see gates-extended.ts's own header comment for why
  // (a real cross-file import, even type-only, breaks this file's
  // CommonJS `require()` at runtime; a real, tsc-enforced local
  // RegimeValidationResult interface is used instead, deliberately
  // duplicating rather than importing types.js's RegimeState).
  //
  // KNOWN, EXPECTED baseline noise on a fresh run (same two categories
  // trade-verdict's own Phase 0 documented — neither is a real bug):
  //   1. Any local `require`/`import` of an untyped sibling file with no
  //      corresponding @typedef will report as implicit `any` — expected
  //      until that file gets its own typedef coverage in a later pass.
  //   2. Generic noise from untyped third-party libraries this repo
  //      depends on (Express/Stripe/Supabase) if anything outside
  //      gates-extended.js's own scope gets pulled in transitively.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noImplicitAny": false,
    "strictNullChecks": false
  },
  "include": ["gates-extended.ts", "analyze-helpers.ts", "types.js"]
}
